  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 6.96,
      "end": 11.97,
      "text": "A ticket arrives. Jev reads it and routes it."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.97,
      "end": 20.99,
      "text": "Venn, with no history, is given plain descriptions of the 77 queues and routes the same ticket."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.99,
      "end": 28.99,
      "text": "Scored on the same 3,080 tickets: Jev 79.7%, Venn without history 69.0%. On day one, use Jev."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.99,
      "end": 35.6,
      "text": "Neither has seen one of this desk's tickets yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.6,
      "end": 41.7,
      "text": "Attach the desk's closed tickets. Nothing is trained; the store is pointed at."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.7,
      "end": 51.22,
      "text": "Every answer now comes with the precedents it used, and how each was resolved."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.22,
      "end": 65.75,
      "text": "The counter moves to 93.6%."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.75,
      "end": 75.91,
      "text": "Five resolved tickets per queue already clear the decision model's interval on this desk; on CLINC150 it takes fifty."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.91,
      "end": 88.59,
      "text": "One embedding of the ticket. From it: the queue, the three precedents, and whether it belongs in the queue it landed in."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.59,
      "end": 99.7,
      "text": "A ticket a legacy rule filed in the wrong queue: the same vector, one more question, and set_membership flags it."
    },
    {
      "start": 99.7,
      "end": 112.84,
      "text": "The registered question, affected by the FX-fee change or not, at threshold 0.9: 5% precision and 9,505 tickets sent to review."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.84,
      "end": 122.84,
      "text": "Re-tag the whole backlog with the 77 queues and file the two FX queues: 361 tickets, 98% precision, 99% recall, 1.9 seconds in process."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.84,
      "end": 133.99,
      "text": "A sweep is as good as its question. The queues the desk already has are the better question."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.99,
      "end": 138.99,
      "text": "\u201cI was NOT charged twice. One charge, but my statement shows two lines.\u201d"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.99,
      "end": 144.99,
      "text": "Venn's precedents say duplicate charge. Jev reads the negation."
    }
  ],
